<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Chromecorp half year eps dives.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Chromecorp half year eps dives.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		12.0	  vs 27.0</p>
<p>NOTE - The firm said it was not paying a dividend as it preferred to use its cash resources to fund capital expenditure.  </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   22.35	 vs 49.39</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   35.32	 vs 75.73</p>
<p>    Tax			 12.97	 vs 26.34</p>
<p>    Interest received     0.99	  vs 0.06</p>
<p>    Turnover		  415.18	vs 311.72</p>
<p>Full name: Chromecorp Ltd (Steel &amp; Allied)</p>
<p>NOTE - The firm said that demand for ferrochrome remained firm and high sales volumes by South African producers would probably persist.</p>
<p>But it added a marginal reduction in stainless steel production was likely to prevent any further significant increase in market prices during the second half of the year.</p>
